  "rules": {
    "QNX001": {
      "title": "epoll event loop",
      "category": "events",
      "base_severity": "high",
      "confidence": "documented",
      "why": "epoll has no page in the QNX 8.0 C Library Reference. The ionotify() page states that it 'corresponds to the Linux epoll() function and BSD's kqueue()'.",
      "qnx_8_0": "Use poll()/ppoll()/select() when you only wait on file descriptors. Use ionotify() with a SIGEV_PULSE event (registered with MsgRegisterEvent()) and receive it with MsgReceivePulse() when the loop must also serve QNX messages, timers or pulses from other threads. ionotify() arms are one-shot: re-arm after every delivery.",
      "docs": [
        {
          "title": "ionotify()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/i/ionotify.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "poll(), ppoll()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/p/poll.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "select(), pselect()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/s/select.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "MsgReceivePulse()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/m/msgreceivepulse.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "MsgRegisterEvent()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/m/msgregisterevent.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "sigevent",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/s/sigevent.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QNX013": {
      "title": "/proc paths (Linux layout)",
      "category": "system",
      "base_severity": "high",
      "confidence": "verify",
      "why": "QNX has a /proc, but it is a process-manager namespace with its own layout, not Linux text files such as /proc/cpuinfo, /proc/meminfo, /proc/stat or /proc/<pid>/stat.",
      "qnx_8_0": "Use the QNX /proc interface (devctl() with DCMD_PROC_* commands) described in the Programmer's Guide, sysconf(), or pidin-style queries instead of parsing Linux files. For the executable path, QNX provides /proc/self/exefile (verify on your target).",
      "docs": [
        {
          "title": "Controlling processes via the /proc filesystem (Programmer's Guide)",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.prog/topic/process_proc_filesystem.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "devctl()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/d/devctl.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QNX035": {
      "title": "systemd / udev integration",
      "category": "system",
      "base_severity": "high",
      "confidence": "verify",
      "why": "<systemd/...> and <libudev.h> are Linux service/device-manager libraries.",
      "qnx_8_0": "Replace service notification and device hotplug with the QNX equivalents for your system: process start-up via your boot scripts or system launch manager, procmgr_daemon() for daemonizing (documented) and QNX device managers. Make the dependency optional (verify design).",
      "docs": [
        {
          "title": "procmgr_daemon()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/p/procmgr_daemon.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QNX008": {
      "title": "CPU affinity",
      "category": "process",
      "base_severity": "high",
      "confidence": "documented",
      "why": "sched_setaffinity / pthread_setaffinity_np and the CPU_* macros have no page in the QNX 8.0 C Library Reference.",
      "qnx_8_0": "For the calling thread use ThreadCtl(_NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK, &mask) (also _NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK_GET_AND_SET and _NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK_GET_AND_SET_INHERIT); map CPU numbers to bits of the runmask. The ThreadCtl() page says the runmask commands can only be executed on the calling thread, so code that sets the affinity of ANOTHER thread or process (sched_setaffinity(pid, ...)) has no documented equivalent: the target thread must set its own runmask (verify). sched_getcpu() has no documented equivalent: verify.",
      "docs": [
        {
          "title": "ThreadCtl()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/t/threadctl.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QNX019": {
      "title": "Linux/glibc preprocessor guards",
      "category": "portability",
      "base_severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "verify",
      "why": "Code under #ifdef __linux__ / __GLIBC__ is not compiled by qcc for QNX, so such branches silently disappear and some #else branches may pick a BSD or generic path that was never tested on QNX.",
      "qnx_8_0": "Add an explicit __QNXNTO__ (and/or __QNX__) branch, or restructure so the portable code path is the default. qcc predefines the QNX macros: confirm with 'qcc -V... -dM -E - < /dev/null' on your SDP (verify).",
      "docs": [
        {
          "title": "qcc / q++ (Utilities Reference)",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.utilities/topic/q/qcc.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QNX023": {
      "title": "accept4 / dup3 / SOCK_* creation flags",
      "category": "io",
      "base_severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "verify",
      "why": "accept4 and dup3 have no page in the QNX 8.0 C Library Reference; SOCK_NONBLOCK/SOCK_CLOEXEC support depends on the network stack headers of your SDP.",
      "qnx_8_0": "Use accept()/dup2()/socket() followed by fcntl(fd, F_SETFD, FD_CLOEXEC) and fcntl(fd, F_SETFL, O_NONBLOCK) (a small wrapper keeps the call sites clean). Note the non-atomic window if you fork concurrently (verify). pipe2() and mkostemp() are documented and can stay.",
      "docs": [
        {
          "title": "pipe(), pipe2()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/p/pipe.html"
        },
        {
          "title": "mkostemp()",
          "url": "https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/8.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.lib_ref/topic/m/mkostemp.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QNX020": {
      "title": "glibc / GNU extensions",
      "category": "portability",
      "base_severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "verify",
      "why": "These GNU extensions have no page in the QNX 8.0 C Library Reference (they may still be available in your SDP headers or not: the compiler is the judge).",
      "qnx_8_0": "Provide a small portable replacement in your own code (strchrnul/memrchr/qsort_r/secure_getenv/canonicalize_file_name/get_current_dir_name are a few lines each), or guard the use. Do not assume the glibc behaviour (verify).",
