    "QNX027": {
      "title": "Linux-only mmap/madvise options",
      "category": "io",
      "base_severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "verify",
      "why": "mmap() on QNX documents MAP_ANON (not MAP_ANONYMOUS), MAP_LAZY, MAP_NORESERVE, MAP_STACK and others; MAP_POPULATE, MAP_HUGETLB, MAP_GROWSDOWN, MAP_LOCKED, MAP_32BIT and mremap() are Linux features.",
      "qnx_8_0": "Use MAP_ANON, drop prefault/huge-page flags (or find the QNX equivalent in the mmap() page), and replace mremap() with mmap + copy. madvise() has no C Library Reference page: use posix_madvise() (documented) (verify).",
